---
import kcAvailability from '../../data/kc-availability.json';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ToolHero from '../../components/tools/ToolHero.astro';
import ToolHowItWorks from '../../components/tools/ToolHowItWorks.astro';
import ToolFAQ from '../../components/tools/ToolFAQ.astro';
import ToolRelatedCTA from '../../components/tools/ToolRelatedCTA.astro';
import ResumeState from '../../components/assessments/ResumeState.astro';

const today = '2026-07-19T00:00:00+00:00';

// Paddle checkout config (publishable values only; the secret API key never touches the build).
// Price id is left empty until Claude Code wires the $29 product; button shows "Coming soon" until then.
const PADDLE_ENV = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PADDLE_ENV || 'sandbox';
const PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN || '';
const PADDLE_CAREER_PRICE = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PADDLE_CAREER_PRICE || '';

// Which of the 8 archetype editions actually have a template PDF to serve.
// DERIVED at build time from the templates that get deployed to the bouncer, never hardcoded:
// an edition turns itself on the moment its PDF lands, and can never be listed before it exists.
// Without this, a buyer in an unbuilt bucket pays at Paddle and only THEN hits the 503 in
// download_handler.php (the template check happens after the money moves). See §13.4.
// The template list is snapshotted by scripts/kc-availability.mjs (paddle-server/ is private, not in CI).
const BUILT_BUCKETS = (kcAvailability.templates || [])
  .map((f) => /^cs-([a-z]+)-template\.pdf$/.exec(f))
  .filter(Boolean)
  .map((m) => m[1])
  .sort(); // no templates listed -> nothing is buyable (fail closed)

const steps = [
  { title: 'Answer about 53 quick questions', description: 'Three short sections (strengths, work-style, and interests) with a progress rail and an elapsed timer. Behavioral questions with no right or wrong answers, plus a quick attention check. Back navigation keeps your answers. About 16 to 18 minutes, with no account and no email.' },
  { title: 'Get your free Work Signature', description: 'See your archetype, your eight strengths ranked on a radar, your five work-style sliders, your interests, and three matched modern roles, all computed in your browser the moment you finish.' },
  { title: 'Act on your matches', description: 'The free result names the roles that fit and how you work best. An optional $29 report adds your top role matches ranked in depth plus a wider modern-role library, each tagged for AI outlook, your blind spots, and a next-90-days plan with resume phrasing.' },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is the Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map is a free assessment that measures your strengths, work-style, and interests across about 53 questions, then names your archetype and matches you to modern roles including remote, gig, and AI-era jobs. It runs entirely in your browser, takes about 16 to 18 minutes, needs no signup, and ends with an optional $29 report. More assessments live in the <a href="/knowledge-center/">Knowledge Center</a>.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the Career Path & Strengths Map free?',
    a: 'Yes. The full on-screen result is completely free with no signup and no email: your archetype, your ranked strengths, your work-style sliders, your interests, and three matched roles. An optional $29 PDF report adds your full role shortlist, blind spots, and a next-90-days plan. The result is never hidden behind a paywall.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is this different from MBTI, CliftonStrengths, or 16Personalities?',
    a: 'MBTI and 16Personalities sort you into fixed personality types that many people fail to reproduce on retake. The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map uses an original framework built on strengths, work-style, and interests, ranked for you rather than boxed into a type, and it maps to real modern roles. The same answers always give the same result.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need to create an account or give my email?',
    a: 'No. No account, email, or signup of any kind is required. Open the page, answer about 53 questions, and your full result appears instantly. There are no email gates and no paywall on the free result. An email is only involved if you choose to buy the optional $29 report, and that is handled by the payment processor.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are my answers stored or sent to a server?',
    a: 'No. Every answer and score is computed inside your browser with client-side JavaScript. Nothing is uploaded, logged, or transmitted. Progress is held only in the tab session memory so a refresh does not lose your place, and it clears when the tab closes. The page even keeps working if you disconnect from the internet after loading.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does the assessment take and how many questions are there?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map has about 53 questions plus a quick attention check, and takes about 16 to 18 minutes. The number of questions and the time are shown before you start, so there are no surprises. Questions are grouped into three sections (strengths, work-style, and interests) with a visible progress rail, and you can go back and change any answer.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I figure out what career I want if I do not know what I am good at?',
    a: 'Start by measuring how you actually work, not by guessing. The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map infers your strengths from behavioral questions (for example, what you do when a project stalls) rather than asking you to rate yourself, then ranks eight strength themes and matches them to roles. Most people surface strengths they had never named.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use this to change careers at 30, 40, or 50?',
    a: 'Yes. The assessment is built for career changers. Instead of your job title, it reads your underlying strengths, work-style, and interests, which transfer across fields, then shows modern roles that fit them. It is designed to reveal where your existing experience carries over, so a mid-career pivot starts from your strengths rather than from zero.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are the signs I am in the wrong career?',
    a: 'Common signs are a job that drains rather than energizes you, work that clashes with how you prefer to operate, and using few of your real strengths day to day. The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map surfaces these by comparing your work-style and interests against the kind of work a role demands, so a mismatch becomes visible instead of just felt.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which careers hold up best as AI changes work?',
    a: 'No career is fully safe, but some strengths stay human-led as AI reshapes work. The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map tags every matched role with an AI outlook, whether AI amplifies the role or its core stays human-led, so you can aim at roles where your human strengths keep their value. This is a read on the direction of travel, not a guarantee, and it is something legacy career tests ignore entirely.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the difference between the free result and the paid report?',
    a: 'The free result is a complete diagnosis: archetype, ranked strengths, work-style, interests, and three sample roles, with nothing held back for an email. The $29 PDF report turns that into a plan: your full strengths ranking with each shadow side, your top role matches ranked in depth plus a wider modern-role library, your blind spots, and a next-90-days plan with resume and LinkedIn phrasing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is my result calculated?',
    a: 'Each question maps to one dimension. Behavioral answers build a score for each of eight strength themes, five work-style sliders, and six interest areas, all shown on a 0 to 100 scale. Your strength themes are then ranked against each other, a within-person (ipsative) ranking rather than a comparison to other people, and your archetype is your top theme. The method is transparent and deterministic: the same answers always produce the same result.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How rigorous is the Career Path & Strengths Map?',
    a: 'It is built on established work-psychology ideas (trait-style dimensions, work values, and interest areas) expressed in an original framework, not a clinical or hiring-grade psychometric. It ranks your own themes against each other (a within-person, or ipsative, profile) rather than against a population, uses multiple questions per dimension, and is deterministic, so the same answers always produce the same result. Treat it as a structured starting point for career thinking, not a validated personality type.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I retake the assessment to track how I change?',
    a: 'Yes, with unlimited free retakes. Every attempt starts fresh with no cached answers, so each result reflects your honest current answers. Because scoring is deterministic, a genuine shift in how you answer is a genuine shift in your result, which makes it a useful check-in when your situation or priorities change over time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What kind of roles does it match me to, including remote and AI jobs?',
    a: 'The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map matches you to a modern role library that legacy tests overlook: remote-first roles, gig and creator paths, and AI-augmented jobs such as AI workflow specialist or prompt designer. Each role is tagged for remote-friendliness and AI outlook, and the free result shows your three closest matches.',
  },
];

const seo = {
  title: 'Career Path & Strengths Map: Free Strengths Test (2026)',
  description: 'Free strengths and career-fit test: about 53 questions, instant result with your archetype and matched modern roles, no signup. Answers stay in your browser.',
  url: '/knowledge-center/career-strengths/',
  type: 'WebPage' as const,
  datePublished: today,
  dateModified: today,
  breadcrumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Knowledge Center', url: '/knowledge-center/' },
    { name: 'Career Path & Strengths Map', url: '/knowledge-center/career-strengths/' },
  ],
  faq: faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, '').replace(/\s{2,}/g, ' ').trim() })),
};
---

<BaseLayout seo={seo}>
  <div id="as-hero">
  <ToolHero
    badge="Free Assessment · No Signup, No Email"
    title="Career Path & Strengths Map:"
    accentText="what are you built for?"
    description="A short, honest map of your real strengths, how you work best, and the modern roles that fit, including remote, gig, and AI-era jobs the old tests ignore. About 53 questions, roughly 16 to 18 minutes. Answers never leave your browser."
    backLink="/knowledge-center/"
    backLabel="Knowledge Center"
  />
  </div>

  <!-- ============ ASSESSMENT ============ -->
  <section class="py-6 md:py-10" aria-label="Career Path and Strengths Map assessment">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">

      <!-- Intro / start card -->
      <div id="as-intro" class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-md p-8 md:p-10 max-w-content mx-auto text-center">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-3">A map of how you actually work</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted max-w-lg mx-auto mb-6">This is not a personality horoscope. It measures your strengths, your work-style, and what genuinely pulls you, then matches you to real modern roles and shows you what to do next.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 mb-7 max-w-md mx-auto">
          <div class="bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm p-3"><span class="block text-xs font-bold text-bae-ink">Strengths</span><span class="block text-[11px] text-bae-muted mt-0.5">8 themes</span></div>
          <div class="bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm p-3"><span class="block text-xs font-bold text-bae-ink">Work-Style</span><span class="block text-[11px] text-bae-muted mt-0.5">5 sliders</span></div>
          <div class="bg-bae-bg border border-bae-border rounded-bae-sm p-3"><span class="block text-xs font-bold text-bae-ink">Interests</span><span class="block text-[11px] text-bae-muted mt-0.5">6 areas</span></div>
        </div>
        <button id="as-start" type="button" class="bg-bae-primary text-white font-semibold text-sm px-8 py-3.5 rounded-bae-sm hover:opacity-90 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5">Start the assessment →</button>
        <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-4 font-medium">about 53 questions + a quick check · roughly 16–18 minutes · no signup, nothing saved · your full result is free</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Optional situation (tailors result framing; never scored) -->
      <div id="as-situation" class="hidden bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-md p-8 md:p-10 max-w-content mx-auto">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-2 text-center">First, where are you right now?</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted text-center max-w-lg mx-auto mb-7">Optional, and takes ten seconds. It only tailors the wording of your result. It never affects your scores, and like everything here it never leaves this browser tab.</p>
        <div id="sit-opts" class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-8 max-w-lg mx-auto"></div>
        <div class="text-center">
          <button id="as-begin" type="button" class="bg-bae-primary text-white font-semibold text-sm px-8 py-3.5 rounded-bae-sm hover:opacity-90 transition-all hover:-translate-y-0.5">Continue to the questions →</button>
          <button id="as-skip" type="button" class="block mx-auto mt-3 text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink underline underline-offset-4">Skip this step</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quiz -->
      <div id="as-quiz" class="hidden">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[250px_1fr] gap-5 items-stretch">
          <aside class="bg-bae-ink rounded-bae p-5 md:p-6 text-white flex flex-col h-full">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-base font-semibold">Your Work Signature</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-4">3 sections · 54 items</p>
            <div id="as-rail"></div>
            <div class="mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-white/10 text-xs text-gray-400">
              Elapsed <b class="text-white tabular-nums" id="as-timer">00:00</b> · <b class="text-white" id="as-pct">0%</b> complete
            </div>
          </aside>
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-md p-6 md:p-9">
            <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary mb-1" id="as-seclabel"></div>
            <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted mb-3">Question <span id="as-num">1</span> of <span id="as-total">54</span></div>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-bae-ink leading-snug mb-1.5" id="as-q"></h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-6" id="as-help"></p>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-2.5" id="as-opts" role="group" aria-label="Answer options"></div>
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center mt-6">
              <button id="as-back" type="button" class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink px-3 py-2 rounded-bae-sm hover:bg-bae-border-light transition-colors disabled:opacity-30">← Back</button>
              <span class="text-xs text-bae-muted hidden sm:inline">Press <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-bae-border-light border border-bae-border rounded text-[11px] font-semibold">1</kbd>–<kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 bg-bae-border-light border border-bae-border rounded text-[11px] font-semibold">4</kbd> to answer</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Calculating interstitial -->
      <div id="as-calc" class="hidden bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-md p-10 md:p-14 max-w-content mx-auto text-center">
        <div class="mx-auto mb-6 w-12 h-12 rounded-full border-[3px] border-bae-border border-t-bae-primary animate-spin" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-bae-ink mb-2">Building your Work Signature</h2>
        <p id="as-calcmsg" class="text-sm text-bae-muted min-h-[1.5rem] transition-opacity duration-300" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="max-w-xs mx-auto mt-6 h-1.5 rounded-full overflow-hidden" style="background:#f0f0f6">
          <i id="as-calcbar" class="block h-full rounded-full bg-bae-primary" style="width:0%;transition:width 1s linear"></i>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-5">All of this happens in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Result -->
      <div id="as-result" class="hidden">
        <div id="as-resulthead" class="text-center mb-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Your free result</span>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-bae-ink mt-1">This is not a horoscope. It is a map of how you work.</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mt-1.5" id="res-stamp"></p>
        </div>

        <div class="w-full">

          <!-- Archetype headline sits ABOVE the split: on phones that lets the buy card fall
               directly under it and above the detail; on desktop the detail and the sticky buy
               rail sit side by side beneath it. -->
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-md p-6 md:p-9">
          <div class="text-center">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-muted">You are</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-bae-primary mt-1 mb-2" id="res-arch">—</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted max-w-xl mx-auto" id="res-archdesc"></p>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-primary mt-2" id="res-note" style="display:none"></p>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-bae-muted mt-2" id="res-situation"></p>
          </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_330px] gap-6 lg:gap-7 items-start mt-6">
          <div class="order-2 lg:order-1 bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-md p-6 md:p-9">

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-center mt-7">
            <div class="text-center">
              <svg id="res-radar" viewBox="0 0 400 320" width="100%" style="max-width:400px" aria-label="Strength radar chart" role="img"></svg>
              <div class="text-xs text-bae-muted mt-1">Your 8 strength themes</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h4 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-1">Your strengths, ranked</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mb-3.5">Your top themes are what to build a career around. <span class="text-bae-primary font-semibold">The paid report adds each one's shadow side, the overuse trap to watch.</span></p>
              <div id="res-strengths" class="flex flex-col gap-2.5"></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 pt-7 border-t border-bae-border-light">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-1">How you work best</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mb-5">No right or wrong end, just how you work best. This is what routes you toward the right kind of role.</p>
            <div id="res-sliders" class="flex flex-col gap-4 max-w-2xl"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 pt-7 border-t border-bae-border-light">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-4">What pulls you</h4>
            <div id="res-interests" class="flex flex-col gap-2.5 max-w-2xl"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 pt-7 border-t border-bae-border-light">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold text-bae-ink mb-1">3 modern roles that fit you</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-bae-muted mb-4">Matched to your strengths and interests, and tagged for remote-friendliness and how AI is changing the role, the thing the legacy tests never tell you. <span class="text-bae-primary font-semibold">The paid report ranks your top matches in depth, with a reason each one fits.</span></p>
            <div id="res-roles" class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3"></div>
          </div>

          </div>

          <!-- Paid CTA. Sticky on desktop so it follows the reader down their result; on phones it
               drops to order-1, directly under the archetype headline. The card MUST stay shorter
               than the viewport or the browser cannot pin it - hence the compact cover. -->
          <aside class="order-1 lg:order-2 lg:sticky lg:top-6">
          <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae shadow-bae-md p-5 md:p-6">
            <div id="res-ctagrid">
              <!-- Live cover preview: the buyer's own edition cover with their real radar drawn on it.
                   Kept compact (158px) so the whole card stays shorter than the viewport and can pin. -->
              <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[158px]">
                <div id="res-cover" class="relative rounded-bae-sm overflow-hidden shadow-xl ring-1 ring-black/20">
                  <img id="res-coverimg" alt="" decoding="async" class="block w-full h-auto select-none" draggable="false" />
                  <svg id="res-coversvg" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full" viewBox="0 0 595.28 841.89" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" aria-hidden="true"></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-center text-[11px] font-medium text-bae-muted mt-2.5">Your personalized cover · 17-page fillable PDF</p>
              </div>
              <!-- Value text + buy button -->
              <div class="mt-4">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Your Career Playbook</span>
                <h4 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-bae-ink mt-1 mb-2">Turn this map into a plan, <span id="res-ctaname" class="text-bae-primary italic">built for you</span></h4>
                <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-1.5 text-[12.5px] font-medium text-bae-ink mt-1">
                  <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-bae-primary font-bold">✓</span> Full strengths ranking, plus each shadow side</li>
                  <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-bae-primary font-bold">✓</span> Your top three matches in depth, plus a wider role library</li>
                  <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-bae-primary font-bold">✓</span> An AI outlook read on every role</li>
                  <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-bae-primary font-bold">✓</span> Your blind spots, named honestly</li>
                  <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-bae-primary font-bold">✓</span> Your five work-style sliders and six interest areas, scored</li>
                  <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-bae-primary font-bold">✓</span> A next-90-days plan with resume phrasing</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="mt-5">
                  <button id="res-buy" type="button" class="block w-full text-center bg-bae-primary text-white font-extrabold text-sm px-6 py-3.5 rounded-bae-sm opacity-90 cursor-default select-none transition hover:opacity-100">Coming soon · $29</button>
                  <span id="res-buynote" class="block text-center text-[11px] font-semibold mt-2 text-bae-muted">One-time · no signup · no subscription</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          </aside>
          </div>

          <div class="text-center mt-6">
            <button id="as-retake" type="button" class="text-sm font-semibold text-bae-muted hover:text-bae-ink underline underline-offset-4">Retake the assessment (fresh start)</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <ToolHowItWorks steps={steps} />
  <ToolFAQ faqs={faqs} />

  <!-- What people map with it -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-bae-border-light">
    <div class="container max-w-page mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-bae-ink mb-2">What people map with it</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted mb-8">Common use cases from career changers, students, and people who feel stuck.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Career Changers</span>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mt-2 mb-1">See where your strengths transfer, not just your job title</h3>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-primary mb-3">Modern roles matched to your profile</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted">A pivot is scary when it feels like starting from zero. The Best Answer Hub Career Path & Strengths Map reads the strengths, work-style, and interests underneath your experience, which carry across fields, then shows the modern roles that fit them, so the next move starts from what you already do well.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Students & New Grads</span>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mt-2 mb-1">Find your direction without needing experience first</h3>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-bae-primary mb-3">No CV required, no signup</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-bae-muted">You do not need a track record to read this. The assessment shows the kind of work that will fit how you think and what pulls you, and points to modern roles worth aiming at, including remote and AI-era jobs that did not exist a few years ago.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bae-card border border-bae-border rounded-bae p-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-bae-primary">Stuck or Burned Out</span>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-bae-ink mt-2 mb-1">Understand why a job that looks fine still drains you</h3>
